Negative control for the refusal being marked ON THE ROW (`H6`/`H10` · `AC6.3`).

Takes the ring off the row and leaves it to the record GROUP. A table row-group is
not a box a browser paints an outline around: the live drive found the errored row
carrying no border, no outline and no shadow at all, while a red hairline landed on
the row ABOVE it. The refused record read as unmarked and its neighbour read as
refused.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the row-ring spec — the invalid ring is on the element that carries
`aria-invalid`, and that element is the row.

